  "content": "<span>Materials</span> <span><span>cramerbn@ornl.gov</span></span> <span><time datetime=\"2026-03-05T10:37:52-05:00\" title=\"Thursday, March 5, 2026 - 10:37\">Thu, 03/05/2026 - 10:37</time> </span> <div class=\"field-wrapper\"> <div class=\"field-container\"> <div class=\"field-element\"> <div class=\"text-only-container\"> <div class=\"field-wrapper text-left-indent\"> <div class=\"field-container\"> <div class=\"field-element\"><h2>America’s most comprehensive materials research program</h2><p>Materials underpin nearly every major scientific and technological breakthrough shaping the nation’s future. From advanced nuclear energy and fusion to quantum computing, space exploration, and modern manufacturing, progress depends on discovering and engineering materials with new capabilities.&nbsp;</p><p>As the nation’s largest multiprogram science and energy laboratory, Oak Ridge National Laboratory brings together an unmatched breadth of expertise to meet this challenge. ORNL integrates quantum-scale research with advanced synthesis, characterization, artificial intelligence, and large-scale computation. This end-to-end capability enables researchers to understand materials at the atomic level and design them for demanding real-world applications.</p><p>These efforts directly support national priorities in energy innovation, defense and nonproliferation, and economic competitiveness, accelerating the transition from discovery to deployment.</p></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"field-element\"> <div class=\"paragraph paragraph--type--multi-column-section paragraph--view-mode--default\"> <h2>Core Capabilities</h2> <div class=\"multi-column-wrapper\"> <div class=\"multi-column-4\"> <div class=\"featured-card\"> <div class=\"featured-card-image\"> <div class=\"field-wrapper\"> <div class=\"field-container\"> <div class=\"field-element\"> <article aria-label=\"Materials conversion.jpg\"> <div class=\"content-image content-image--undefined\"> <div class=\"content-image__img\"> <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://www.ornl.gov/sites/default/files/styles/main_image_style/public/2025-07/Materials%20conversion.jpg?h=ae1281eb&amp;itok=WJUXDlom\" width=\"1000\" height=\"650\" alt=\"A close-up view of a hand in a purple glove holding a small, metal tube with black materials spilling out.\"> <div class=\"content-image__magnify\"> <a href=\"https://www.ornl.gov/sites/default/files/2025-07/Materials%20conversion.jpg\"><span>View a hi-res version of this image</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </article> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"featured-card-text\"> <div class=\"featured-card-heading\"> <div class=\"field-wrapper\"> <div class=\"field-container\"> <div class=\"field-element\">Materials Discovery &amp; Synthesis</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"field-wrapper\"> <div class=\"field-container\"> <div class=\"field-element\"><p>Discovering and creating new materials with tailored properties for energy, security, and advanced manufacturing applications.</p></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"featured-card\"> <div class=\"featured-card-image\"> <div class=\"field-wrapper\"> <div class=\"field-container\"> <div class=\"field-element\"> <article aria-label=\"CNMS.png\"> <div class=\"content-image content-image--undefined\"> <div class=\"content-image__img\"> <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://www.ornl.gov/sites/default/files/styles/main_image_style/public/2026-02/CNMS.png?h=8b61671e&amp;itok=decYpwdm\" width=\"1000\" height=\"650\" alt=\"An image of an imaging system at CNMS\"> <div class=\"content-image__magnify\"> <a href=\"https://www.ornl.gov/sites/default/files/2026-02/CNMS.png\"><span>View a hi-res version of this image</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </article> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"featured-card-text\"> <div class=\"featured-card-heading\"> <div class=\"field-wrapper\"> <div class=\"field-container\"> <div class=\"field-element\">Characterization &amp; Neutron Science</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"field-wrapper\"> <div class=\"field-container\"> <div class=\"field-element\"><p>Using world-leading neutron sources and advanced instrumentation to probe materials at the atomic scale and understand structure, dynamics, and performance.</p></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"featured-card\"> <div class=\"featured-card-image\"> <div class=\"field-wrapper\"> <div class=\"field-container\"> <div class=\"field-element\"> <article aria-label=\"AI-revamps-materials-synthesis-modeling-thumbnail-720x540.jpg\"> <div class=\"content-image content-image--undefined\"> <div class=\"content-image__img\"> <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://www.ornl.gov/sites/default/files/styles/main_image_style/public/2024-09/AI-revamps-materials-synthesis-modeling-thumbnail-720x540.jpg?h=a1f525db&amp;itok=yP4H_MQ2\" width=\"1000\" height=\"650\" alt=\"pulsed laser deposition setup\"> <div class=\"content-image__magnify\"> <a href=\"https://www.ornl.gov/sites/default/files/2024-09/AI-revamps-materials-synthesis-modeling-thumbnail-720x540.jpg\"><span>View a hi-res version of this image</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </ar",
